<task>
Explain what the following git changes do in clear, plain language.
</task>

<context>
<refs>
${GIT_DIFF_REFS}
</refs>

<branch>
${GIT_BRANCH}
</branch>

<diffstat>
${GIT_DIFF_STAT}
</diffstat>

<diff>
${GIT_DIFF}
</diff>

<commits>
${GIT_COMMITS}
</commits>
</context>

${GIT_EXPLAIN_DESCRIPTION}

<instructions>
First review the diff to understand what changed, then group the changes
logically, and finally assess the intent and impact.
</instructions>

<rules>
- Focus on what changed and why, not how.
- Organize by logical change groups, not by files.
- If the diff appears incomplete or truncated, state that limitation.
- If no commits are listed, the changes are unstaged or staged but not committed.
</rules>

<output_format>
Format: GitHub-flavored Markdown
Output only the explanation.
Do not include preamble or a title.
Omit sections that are not relevant to the input.

<example>
## Summary
{one or two sentence overview}

## What Changed
{grouped logical changes with brief explanation of each}

## Why
{inferred intent, if clearly supported by the diff}
</example>
</output_format>
